g> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/205274-stigmatic-and-demon-blooded-character-sheets?p=640982#post640982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One quick thing though, Is it &quot;Stigma&quot;? Or &quot;Stigmata&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stigma is the proper singular, stigmata is the plural. More people are familiar with the plural when speaking of the definition we're working with, so it's often used as the singular as well. The books refer to a stigmatic's signature glitch as &quot;stigmata,&quot; but it's unclear whether they're speaking in the singular, or collectively as a plural (like referring to one glitch manifesting multiple times and ways).<br /> <br /> The confusion's probably my fault for using it up-thread! It's more my personal preference than anything official.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T16:35:36-07:00","id":666166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/205274-stigmatic-and-demon-blooded-character-sheets?p=640982#post640982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"